{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multimodal interaction multimodal interaction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md","fileName":"Multimodal Interaction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multimodal Interaction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]] · [[Conversational Assistant Design]] · [[Tangible and Multimodal Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Conversational Assistant Design","Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","System Control","Cognitive Load","Dialog Manager","Conversation Context","Gesture Interaction","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","aiassistants.epub","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multimodal interaction multimodal interaction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md","fileName":"Multimodal Interaction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multimodal Interaction","heading":"Multimodal Interaction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Multimodal interaction combines multiple input or output channels in one interface. A person may switch between modalities or use them together, such as speaking a command while pointing to its spatial arguments.\n\nMultiple channels can decouple [[System Control]] from a primary task, resolve ambiguous speech or gestures, support complementary strengths, and give users alternatives when one channel is blocked. They can also increase [[Cognitive Load]] or disrupt the flow of action if switching and coordination are poorly designed.\n\nThe task should be matched to suitable modalities, transitions should be clear, and combined performance should be evaluated rather than assumed to improve automatically.\n\nIn a virtual assistant, speech can be combined with a display, touch, gaze, or physical orientation. The [[Dialog Manager]] must keep these channels in one [[Conversation Context]] so expressions such as “that one” can be resolved against what the user sees or indicates.\n\nAn AR interface can combine speech with [[Gesture Interaction|gesture]], touch, tracked objects, gaze, and haptic output in the same physical frame. One modality can disambiguate another—for example, a spoken command can name an operation while a pointing gesture identifies the situated object to which it applies.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Conversational Assistant Design","Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","System Control","Cognitive Load","Dialog Manager","Conversation Context","Gesture Interaction","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","aiassistants.epub","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multimodal interaction multimodal interaction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multimodal Interaction.md","fileName":"Multimodal Interaction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multimodal Interaction","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n\n[[aiassistants.epub]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Conversational Assistant Design","Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","System Control","Cognitive Load","Dialog Manager","Conversation Context","Gesture Interaction","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","aiassistants.epub","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}